# Third-party notices

The text of this skill is adapted from the DeepSeek Harness skill `dsh-ci-test-reliability` and generalized to reliable tests in CI or an equivalent test lane.

- Upstream: <https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness>, pinned at `dsh-v0.2.3-alpha.2` (`4b399c39a6d1479cd84ca591b4d7c88e24d38a96`).
- Upstream paths:
  - `.agents/skills/dsh-ci-test-reliability/SKILL.md` — the reliability procedure.
  - `.agents/skills/dsh-ci-test-reliability/references/ci-flake-diagnosis.md` — the diagnosis workflow.
- Relation: adapted. The execution-topology, resource-allocation, global-state, platform, timeout, synchronization, teardown, regression-proof and flake-masking rules are carried. Product names, framework and CI-provider assumptions, repository paths and command names are replaced by the adopting project's declared test configuration, CI or equivalent test-lane topology and check-selection practice. The target also treats deterministic test-lane duration as design feedback: it separates fast contracts from one shared expensive scenario and restricts repeated external work to lanes where the result can differ; it does not claim production performance. The description is generalized and Chinese trigger terms are added. The skill ships no script and depends on no other skill.

